            <ArticleTitle>Piloleiomyoma with segmental distribution--Case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>178-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1590/abd1806-4841.20153769</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0365-05962015000700178</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Piloleiomyoma is an uncommon benign neoplasm arising from the erector pilorum muscle. It presents as reddish-brown papules or nodules, in general located on the limbs or trunk, often painful. The present paper describes a case of piloleiomyoma with segmental distribution on left trunk, with an important expression of pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
